cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Nepal Cryosphere Inventory
message: >-
  If you use this inventory, please cite it and, separately, every upstream
  dataset listed under references. This is a derived work.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Ghimire
    given-names: Prajwal
    email: prajwal.1.ghimire@kcl.ac.uk
    affiliation: King's College London
repository-code: 'https://github.com/prazg/Nepal_Cryosphere_Inventory'
url: 'https://prazg.github.io/Nepal_Cryosphere_Inventory/'
abstract: >-
  An open inventory of 4,480 glaciers (4,215 km2 of ice) and 1,429 glacial
  lakes (81 km2) in Nepal, joining RGI 7.0 outlines, ITS_LIVE annual surface
  velocity to 2025, two independent glacial lake inventories, and the HMAGLOFDB
  record of outburst floods. Includes a lake-terminating flag for 201 glaciers,
  which RGI 7.0 itself leaves unassigned for this region.
keywords:
  - glaciers
  - glacial lakes
  - GLOF
  - Nepal
  - Himalaya
  - cryosphere
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-09-01'
version: 1.0.0
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: Randolph Glacier Inventory 7.0
    authors: [{name: RGI Consortium}]
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.5067/f6jmovy5navz
  - type: dataset
    title: ITS_LIVE glacier surface velocity
    authors: [{name: NASA MEaSUREs ITS_LIVE project}]
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      Inventory of Glacial Lakes in High Mountain Asia for the Periods
      2016-2017 and 2022-2024
    authors: [{family-names: Kumar, given-names: Ravindra},
              {family-names: Vijay, given-names: Saurabh}]
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.17948783
  - type: dataset
    title: Annual 30 m dataset for glacial lakes in High Mountain Asia 2008-2017
    authors: [{family-names: Chen, given-names: Fang}]
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.5194/essd-13-741-2021
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      A comprehensive and version-controlled database of glacial lake outburst
      floods in High Mountain Asia
    authors: [{family-names: Shrestha, given-names: Finu}]
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.5194/essd-15-3941-2023
